INT. COUNTY COURTHOUSE - STAIRWELL LANDING - DAY

A marble stairwell that echoes. Dusty light through tall windows. ATTORNEY NAOMI PEMBERTON-CLARKE (40s, charcoal suit, folder) climbs two steps at a time. Behind her trots her junior, DEVANTE OYELOWO (20s, rolled sleeves, briefcase).

                    NAOMI
          Devante, we have eight minutes.

                    DEVANTE
          Ms. Pemberton-Clarke, the witness isn't here yet.

                    NAOMI
          She'll be here.

They reach the landing. A heavyset man waits at the window: JUDGE REGINALD "REGGIE" ABERNATHY (60s, robe over arm), eating a sandwich.

                    REGGIE
          Counsel.

                    NAOMI
          Your Honor.

                    REGGIE
          You're in my stairwell.

                    NAOMI
          We're passing through.

                    DEVANTE
          Sorry, sir. We didn't know it was private.

                    REGGIE
          It isn't. I just like the quiet.

Naomi and Devante glance at each other. Reggie wipes crumbs from his sleeve.

                    REGGIE (CONT'D)
          Tell me, Ms. Pemberton-Clarke. Is your client going to take the stand?

                    NAOMI
          I can't discuss strategy with the bench, Judge.

                    REGGIE
          Of course not.

He tosses the sandwich wrapper at a bin, and misses. They all three stare at it. Devante dives for the wrapper, and Naomi dives for the same one. They collide at the bin. The folder spills. Papers slide across the marble.

                    REGGIE (CONT'D)
          (mildly)
          Well, now I know what's in the file.

Naomi and Devante freeze on their knees. Reggie picks up one page, reads it, and folds it.

                    REGGIE (CONT'D)
          Eight minutes, counsel. I'd hurry.

He walks down the stairs, leaving the page tucked in his pocket.
